      Have you tried setting the number_pad option to 2 instead of
just 1?  That makes the '5' digit behave as a 'g' movement prefix
instead of the 'G' behavior you're observing.  Or you could just
switch to the vi-style movement and let 5 go back to meaning 4+1
as it's supposed to.

      If tweaking number_pad works, note that it is one of the
terminal- and display-specific settings which isn't stored in the
save file, so you'll need to reset it every time you resume play
unless/until they get the run-time configuration file use going.

